At: position]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"values(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" read the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"base’s edge maps too. A view whose positions are not the base’s, such as a complement, has no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"edge-map reads. These members are read-only. A ","type":"text"},{"code":"GraphDelegator","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" writes maps through members","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of its own.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A view whose vertices are a subset of its base’s should declare its own ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[map, of: vertex]"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that traps on a vertex outside the view. The default reads the base’s value.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Nothing else is forwarded. A view’s graph members are its own, or the protocol defaults over","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its own members. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GraphDelegator"},{"text":" forwards every read member to the base, and only a wrapper","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that keeps the base’s adjacency conforms to it. For a view such as a transposed one, the base’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"members would describe the wrong graph.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"inheritedBy","kind":"relationships","title":"Inherited By","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/GraphDelegator"]},{"type":"conformingTypes","kind":"relationships","title":"Conforming Types","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedView","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/UndirectedView"]}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"title":"GraphAdaptor","modules":[{"name":"GraphProtocols"}],"symbolKind":"protocol"